    "title": "pandas.PeriodIndex.day_of_week — pandas 3.1.0.dev0+1386.gcb2086a1a4 documentation",
    "status": 200,
    "markdown": "# pandas.PeriodIndex.day_of_week#\n\n- property PeriodIndex.day_of_week[source]#\n- The day of the week with Monday=0, Sunday=6. Returns the day-of-week component for each period, following the Python convention where Monday is 0 and Sunday is 6. See also \n  - `PeriodIndex.day`\n  - The days of the period.\n  - `PeriodIndex.day_of_week`\n  - The day of the week with Monday=0, Sunday=6.\n  - `PeriodIndex.day_of_year`\n  - The ordinal day of the year.\n  - `PeriodIndex.dayofweek`\n  - The day of the week with Monday=0, Sunday=6.\n  - `PeriodIndex.dayofyear`\n  - The ordinal day of the year.\n  - `PeriodIndex.week`\n  - The week ordinal of the year.\n  - `PeriodIndex.weekday`\n  - The day of the week with Monday=0, Sunday=6.\n  - `PeriodIndex.weekofyear`\n  - The week ordinal of the year.\n Examples >>> idx = pd.PeriodIndex([\"2023-01-01\", \"2023-01-02\", \"2023-01-03\"], freq=\"D\") >>> idx.day_of_week Index([6, 0, 1], dtype='int64')",
